# probe3 under qemu-system-mips -- 2026-09-01

host        Linux 6.6.87.2-microsoft-standard-WSL2
qemu        QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18)
toolchain   mips-linux-gnu-gcc (Ubuntu 12.4.0-2ubuntu1~24.04) 12.4.0
machine     -M malta -m 32 -nographic -kernel <elf> -serial file:
seconds     120 (nothing here halts; the run is bounded by timeout)

# WHY THERE IS A THIRD ONE OF THESE.  The 2026-08-26 record describes a
# 29,088-byte payload at RB_WORDS = 641 and the 2026-08-31 one a 29,680-byte
# payload at 707.  The eighteenth session added Group F -- the memory-mapped SPI
# window, docs/probe3-cells.md § 6.8 -- so neither describes the image and
# neither capture came from this payload.  All three records are kept, which is
# what the rebuild-on-the-day table in docs/probe3-cells.md means by a moved
# sha256.

## the DEVICE build -- the image that will be uploaded
    payload    build/probe3/probe3.bin
    load addr  0x80500000      entry is byte 0 of the image
    size       31536 bytes
    sha256     fc7b21d479478fcb925723237323176adc7946502a0e71588ae799a626e2824e
    first word 3c1d8051   (must be the first instruction of _start)
    reset      RESET=1   1 = arm the watchdog and hand the prompt back with no power cycle
    flags      50010002   header word 5, and the banner prints it
    flush      CCTL 0x002 -- measured sufficient, R1d decision 1. Not a knob
    isc        ISC=0   1 = rlx_isc_inv is linked. probe2/probe3 must be 0
    template   0x80500ed0 .. 0x80500ed8   the two-word victim, GUARD FIRST
    cp3 stubs  0x80500fa0   eight, 12 bytes each
    outside I  5 cache op(s) + 8 mfc3 -- every word in this image that
               is not MIPS-I. tools/test-rlxprobe.sh names each one and
               fails if the set changes -- probe1/probe2 assert zero, and
               probe3 cannot, because executing them IS question (c).
    stale check the banner must read  rb=80a02000  -- LOWER case, because
               report.c s digit table is 0123456789abcdef while the loader s
               is upper. rb=80a00000 or rb=80a01000 means this image is a
               probe1/probe2-based build and is about to poison a measurement.
    result     RESULT_BASE=0x80A02000   read it back with: DW 80A02000 718
    geom       GEOM=0   base 0x80B00000   1 = ARMED, and it can write 1 MiB
    uart       THR 0xB8002000  LSR 0xB8002014
    vectors    UTLB 0x80000000  general 0x80000080   CLEAR_BEV=0
    hazlint    0 violations in 946 loads (874 at RB_WORDS = 707, 804 at 641)
    bss        _bss_start 0x80507B30  _bss_end 0x80507E20  _stack_top 0x8050BE20
               -- the card reads the first two back with `DW 8050000C 1`, which
               LDR-07 rounds up to four words, so one command carries both.

## the qemu build -- NOT the same image
    UART_THR=0xB80003F8 UART_LSR=0xB80003FD VEC_GENERAL=0x80000180
    CLEAR_BEV=1 RET_ERET=1
    Unchanged from 2026-08-26: three constants differ and nothing else.

## what this run is evidence FOR, and it is narrow
    Control flow only -- qemu interlocks the load delay slot and this core
    does not.  What it shows about Group F is exactly two things, and the
    second one is the more valuable:

      f.alias=00000002         the two windows were both READ and compared
      f.live=0000000f          🔴 THE WIN BYTE IS ZERO.  Malta has no flash at
                               0x1D000000, so 0xBD000000 returned sixteen
                               identical words -- a floating bus -- and that is
                               precisely the refutation condition § 6.8.3
                               writes for a dead window.  IT FIRED, in the only
                               environment that can drive it.  The boot byte is
                               15: Malta DOES have something at 0x1FC00000.
      f.sfcr=ffffffff          no SPI controller at 0xB8001200 either
      f.win.seq .. f.win.seq2  all deadc0de -- see below
      f.faults=00000000        nothing trapped; the reads returned garbage
                               rather than raising, which is Malta's behaviour
                               for unassigned memory and not the device's
      rb.words=000002ce        718
      cells.run=0000000f       15, one more than the 707-word payload

## 🔴 the gate this run found, and it is why the seven legs are poison
    The FIRST build of Group F ran its seven timing legs unconditionally, and
    under qemu they all returned 00000000 -- Malta has no TC0CNT, both bracket
    reads come back all-ones, and the difference of two equal numbers is zero.
    SEVEN ZEROS IS A NUMBER, NOT A REFUSAL, and Group T had already declared
    itself VOID two stages earlier.

    Group V is gated on `c-A` and Groups M and X on `h-brk`; a timing group with
    no gate was this payload disagreeing with its own design.  `if (g_timer)`
    now guards the legs and leaves them at stage 0's poison -- the payload's own
    representation of *this cell did not run* -- and the UART says so:

      rlxprobe: Group F timing VOID -- Group T did not ship, so a tick is not
      a unit on this machine. f-alias and f-live still ran

    tools/rbcheck.py C31 accepts all seven poisoned as a refusal and C32 fails a
    MIX of poisoned and written legs, because a mix is the only one of the three
    that is a bug.

## what it is NOT evidence for
    Every band in § 6.8.2 is about SPI clocks on this silicon.  qemu has no SPI
    controller, no flash window and no timer, so this run cannot narrow FW-34 by
    one bit.  It says the code executes and the gate works.
